ric Tonnes of CO2 Equivalent)**:\n   - Scope-1: 25.44 million tonnes\n   - Scope-2: 59.67 million tonnes\n5. **Non-Current Assets**: Rs. 1,64,005 crore\n6. **Current Assets**: Rs. 96,193 crore\n7. **Dividend Payout Ratio**: 46.19%\n8. **Return on Average Capital Employed**: 22.86%\n9. **Net Profit Margin on Net Sales**: 27.81%\n\n### Analysis:\n- ITC Limited shows a significantly higher profit for the year (Rs. 35,195.61 crore) compared to Coal India Limited, which does not provide direct profit figures. ITC's comprehensive income is also higher (Rs. 34,266.23 crore) and its retained earnings at the end of the year are much higher (Rs. 47,735.79 crore).\n- Coal India Limited focuses on production and operational metrics, such as coal production and greenhouse gas emissions, but does not provide a direct profit figure for the year.\n\n### Conclusion:\nBased on the provided financial data, ITC Limited performed better than Coal India Limited for the year ended 31 March 2026, as ITC showed higher profits and retained earnings.\n\n{\n  \"answer_kind\": \"comparison\",\n  \"answer_value\": \"ITC Limited\",\n  \"unit\": \"crores\",\n  \"period\": \"year ended 31 March 2026\",\n  \"basis\": \"profit for the year and retained earnings\",\n  \"citations\": [\"document_id=2a51bc137e460a2549785e784465e6fe1aa7bcd2ca1077d6e2d2465efdd27acc page=64\", \"document_id=9b63fc3453960fa251c3596f6f1268274d3a159e335acbe9528ca1e3c76e67b1 page=26\"],\n  \"abstain\": false,\n  \"reason\": \"ITC Limited showed higher profits and retained earnings compared to Coal India Limited, which did not provide direct profit figures.\"\n}", "status": "answered", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 949, "prompt_tokens": 1965, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "total_tokens": 2914}}, {"http_status": 200, "latency_ms": 11774, "output": "**Step-by-Step Reasoning:**\n\n1. **Identify the Entities and Timeframe:** The question asks to compare ITC and Coal India for the year ended 31 March 2026, using consolidated figur